okens": 2079, "total_tokens": 2079}}, "input": {"input": ["KARJALUOTO:Karjaluoto is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of mobile banking", "THAKUR:Thakur is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of mobile banking", "BARNES, S. J.:Barnes, S. J. is a researcher who has defined mobile banking as a channel for customer interaction with banks via mobile devices", "CORBITT, B.:Corbitt, B. is a researcher who has defined mobile banking as a channel for customer interaction with banks via mobile devices", "SUORANTA, M.:Suoranta, M. is a researcher who has defined mobile banking as a method of conducting financial services using mobile communication techniques", "MATTILA, M.:Mattila, M. is a researcher who has defined mobile banking as a method of conducting financial services using mobile communication techniques", "ŚWIECKA, B.:Świecka, B. is a researcher who has defined mobile banking as a form of service offered by banks using portable devices", "WIELKOPOLSKI BANK KREDYTOWY:Wielkopolski Bank Kredytowy, now known as Santander Bank Polska, was a pioneer in mobile banking in Poland, introducing SMS notifications for account operations in 1999 and WAP-based mobile banking in 2000", "SANTANDER BANK POLSKA:Santander Bank Polska, formerly known as Wielkopolski Bank Kredytowy, is a prominent financial institution in Poland. The bank has established itself as a leader in the development and provision of mobile banking services, catering to the evolving needs of its customers. Santander Bank Polska offers a comprehensive suite of mobile payment systems, including BLIK, Google Pay, Apple Pay, Garmin Pay, and Fitbit Pay, ensuring that customers have access to a wide range of convenient and secure payment options. The bank's support for BLIK services is particularly noteworthy, as it includes functionalities such as contactless payments, which enhance the ease and efficiency of transactions for its users. Through its commitment to innovation and customer service, Santander Bank Polska continues to play a significant role in the Polish banking sector.", "MBANK:mBank is a prominent financial institution in Poland, recognized as a leader in mobile banking services. Established as a pioneer in the field, mBank introduced WAP-based mobile banking as early as 2000, marking its commitment to technological advancement. The bank has played a significant role in the development of mobile banking and the Polish Standard of Payments, contributing to the creation of the BLIK payment system alongside five other banks. Since 2015, mBank has been offering BLIK services to its customers, further solidifying its position in the mobile payment landscape.\n\nmBank provides a comprehensive suite of mobile banking services, catering to a large user base that includes 2.59 million active mobile app users and 3.95 million individual clients. The bank's mobile application is frequently analyzed for its usage metrics, reflecting its importance in the digital banking sector. mBank offers a variety of mobile payment systems, including BLIK, Google Pay, Apple Pay, Garmin Pay, Fitbit Pay, Swatch PAY!, and Xiaomi Pay, ensuring that customers have access to a wide range of convenient payment options.\n\nSecurity is a top priority for mBank, which offers advanced mobile banking login methods such as PIN, fingerprint, face scan, and iris scan technologies. These features underscore the bank's commitment to providing secure and user-friendly banking experiences. The inclusion of unique features like retina scan login further highlights mBank's dedication to innovation in mobile banking security.\n\nOverall, mBank stands out as a major Polish bank that not only provides extensive mobile banking services but also actively contributes to the evolution of mobile payment systems in Poland. Its leadership in mobile banking, combined with a strong focus on security and customer convenience, positions mBank as a key player in the financial industry.", "INTELIGO:Inteligo is a banking service that introduced the first SIM Toolkit application \"Płacę SMS w Inteligo\" in 2002 and a lite service in 2008", "RAIFFEISEN BANK POLSKA:Raiffeisen Bank Polska is a bank that launched a Java-based mobile application \"R-Mobile\" in 2004 and was the first to offer a mobile app on iOS in 2009", "ALIOR BANK:Alior Bank is a prominent financial institution based in Poland, known for its comprehensive range of mobile banking services and innovative payment solutions. Established as a forward-thinking bank, Alior Bank launched its mobile application in 2010, marking its commitment to digital transformation and customer convenience. The bank offers a variety of mobile banking login methods, including PIN, fingerprint, and face scan, ensuring secure and easy access for its users.\n\nDespite its innovative offerings, Alior Bank has been noted to have lower than average mobile banking indicators. However, it is part of a group with a high percentage of 'mobile only' users, indicating a strong focus on mobile banking solutions. This focus is further exemplified by its extensive mobile payment systems, which include BLIK, Google Pay, Apple Pay, Garmin Pay, Fitbit Pay, and Swatch PAY!, catering to a wide range of customer preferences and enhancing the ease of transactions.\n\nAlior Bank has been a key player in the development and implementation of the BLIK payment system, a significant milestone in Poland's banking sector. As one of the six banks involved in the creation of BLIK, Alior Bank has been offering these services since 2015. BLIK services provided by the bank include contactless payments and other functionalities, demonstrating Alior Bank's commitment to providing cutting-edge financial solutions to its customers.\n\nIn summary, Alior Bank stands out as a dynamic and innovative bank in Poland, offering a robust suite of mobile banking and payment services. Its involvement in the creation and promotion of the BLIK payment system highlights its role as a leader in the digital banking landscape, despite facing challenges with mobile banking indicators. Through its diverse payment options and secure mobile access methods, Alior Bank continues to enhance the banking experience for its customers, solidifying its position in the Polish financial market.", "BANK MILLENNIUM:Bank Millennium is a prominent financial institution in Poland, recognized for its innovative approach to banking technology. Since 2011, the bank has been at the forefront of mobile banking, offering a range of applications that cater to the evolving needs of its customers. As a pioneer in the digital banking space, Bank Millennium has played a significant role in the development of mobile banking applications and the Polish Standard of Payments.\n\nThe bank is particularly noted for its involvement in the creation and implementation of the BLIK payment system, a collaborative effort among six major banks in Poland. BLIK is a mobile payment system that allows users to make contactless payments and perform various other financial transactions with ease and security. Bank Millennium's participation in this initiative underscores its commitment to enhancing the convenience and efficiency of banking services for its clients.\n\nIn addition to BLIK, Bank Millennium offers a variety of mobile payment options, including HCE (Host Card Emulation), Apple Pay, and Garmin Pay. These services reflect the bank's dedication to providing versatile and accessible payment solutions, ensuring that customers can choose the method that best suits their lifestyle and preferences.\n\nOverall, Bank Millennium stands out as a leader in the Polish banking sector, continually advancing its technological offerings to meet the demands of a digital-first world. Through its innovative services and strategic collaborations, the bank remains committed to delivering exceptional value and convenience to its customers.", "BZ WBK:BZ WBK, now known as Santander Bank Polska, has played a significant role in the evolution of banking technology in Poland. The bank was at the forefront of mobile banking innovations, launching its mobile banking applications as early as 2011. This early adoption of mobile technology positioned BZ WBK as a pioneer in the digital banking landscape, catering to the growing demand for convenient and accessible banking solutions.\n\nIn addition to its advancements in mobile banking, BZ WBK was one of the six banks instrumental in the creation of the BLIK payment system. BLIK is a Polish mobile payment system that allows users to make payments and withdraw cash using their mobile devices, further cementing the bank's commitment to enhancing digital financial services. Through its involvement in BLIK, BZ WBK contributed to the development of a robust and innovative payment infrastructure in Poland, which has become widely adopted by consumers and merchants alike.\n\nOverall, BZ WBK's initiatives in mobile banking and its participation in the establishment of the BLIK payment system highlight its dedication to technological advancement and customer-centric banking solutions. Now operating as Santander Bank Polska, the bank continues to build on this legacy, striving to deliver cutting-edge financial services to its customers.", "CITI HANDLOWY:Citi Handlowy is a prominent financial institution in Poland, recognized for its comprehensive mobile banking services. The bank has been at the forefront of digital banking innovation, being part of the initial group of banks to offer mobile banking applications, which it began providing in 2011. Citi Handlowy offers a variety of secure mobile banking login methods, including traditional password, PIN, fingerprint, and face scan, ensuring a high level of security and convenience for its users.\n\nIn addition to its robust mobile banking application, Citi Handlowy supports a range of mobile payment systems, including BLIK, Google Pay, and Apple Pay. The bank has been offering BLIK services since 2021, further enhancing its digital payment solutions. These offerings reflect Citi Handlowy's commitment to providing versatile and modern banking options to its customers.\n\nCiti Handlowy is part of a group of banks in Poland characterized by moderate mobile banking indicators, with an average level of mobile banking adoption among its customers. The bank's mobile application usage metrics have been analyzed, indicating a steady engagement with its digital services. As one of the four banks in Group 3, Citi Handlowy continues to focus on expanding its digital footprint and improving the mobile banking experience for its clientele.\n\nOverall, Citi Handlowy stands out as a key player in the Polish banking sector, leveraging technology to enhance customer experience and maintain its competitive edge in the rapidly evolving financial landscape."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_736bc024e3fa212c9a5f055bfe6d017e119e72d6e6c98791a8bdb79334f29db7_v2"}